finding: P1 — Stage 4's statistical acceptance claim is not established. bin/step.ts uses 59 runs (correct for a single 0.95/0.95 Bernoulli quantity), but SPREAD_FACTOR=10 is retained as an unexplained safety factor for thousands of comparisons, not a distribution-free simultaneous correction. Under Sohier section 5 no distribution-free tail probability follows from multiplying a sampled bound by 10. State a family and error budget before sampling: e.g. for M quantities Bonferroni confidence allocation gives n >= ceil(log(0.05/M)/log(0.95)); ensuring probability for the whole future vector also requires a joint event (or allocating the probability budget, not merely confidence). Additionally stepWithSpread uses only runs with identical discrete outcomes for spread/vectors, potentially fewer than 59, while claiming the same bound; decision occurrences also omit unmatched observations. Specify conditional guarantees with actual sample counts or use an unconditional joint statistic. The 1,579,602 humanoid quantities cannot inherit schedule-wide 95/95 from this implementation. This can remain wrong with every scene and fault probe green. P1 — Coverage falls short of the promised random rounding at every floating-point operation. buildStepOracleMca instruments arithmetic but leaves sqrt and libm at RN (explicitly acknowledged). Inspection of the pinned image's Box3D finds sqrtf in vector normalization (math_functions.h:281,295), quaternion normalization (:517), twist decomposition (:577-578), and b3ComputeCosSin's normalization (math_functions.c:269). These are step-relevant, not unused library calls: randomized surrounding arithmetic does not sample rounding of the sqrt result at fixed operands. Either instrument those sites too, or supply evidence/bounds for this missing noise and explicitly narrow the claim; a vector-width diagnostic alone does not establish this coverage. P2 — The required independent-mean regression is red in isolation. Twice reproduced with bun test test/step.test.ts --test-name-pattern 'randomly rounded runs differ' (and once with the broader three-test filter): test/step.test.ts:305 expected <=0, received 2.525620546034446e-10. The separate IEEE-mode/native comparison passed all 177 runs. A second set is not mathematically guaranteed inside the first sample maximum, especially sohierBound(0)=0; diagnose the nonzero second-set change rather than fitting a floor after seeing this scene. Independently examined the full unit and gpu-physics plan, supplied commit messages and diffs, build/backend/client/statistics, comparison and tests, pinned Docker source and local Verificarlo instrumentation/docs. Narrow GPU fault test filter 'goes red': all four tests pass (faults rejected, floor diagnostics), 67.8 s. Perturb/perturbScene/SPREAD_DIRECTIONS/SPREAD_SCALE are removed from the step implementation; norm/angle and stage-injection additions show no separate finding on inspection. Notes/uncertainty: Docker is working locally (aarch64/Colima); the dependency is unconditional on first spread. Hosted ubuntu has Docker conventionally, but hosted CI was not exercised; workflow has no explicit image provisioning, and this unlanded package points at a Mac-absolute oracle worktree, so local evidence is not CI portability evidence. No pre-land check or full schedules run; humanoid remains test.todo and its reported 1500-step hold was not independently repeated. Source: Sohier et al. arXiv:1807.09655 section 5/Table 3; /private/tmp/verificarlo docs and libVFCInstrument.cpp; pinned image f024f8e3....
